  "body": "We should make the [drag data store mode](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dnd.html#drag-data-store-mode) should be readable when dispatching `dragenter`, `dragleave`, and `dragexit` events. This is what Gecko implements.\r\n\r\nHowever, WebKit and Blink only allows reading of types, and this is a hard platform requirement on iOS for privacy reasons since the apps are not allowed to see the contents of the pasteboard (a.k.a. clipboard) until the drop happens.\r\n\r\nGiven that, I suggest we add new \"types only\" mode to the drag data store mode, and then use it in `dragenter`, `dragleave`, and `dragexit`.",
